"gw.hintTsnetOnly" = "⚠️ This address is reachable only by devices in the same tailnet (logged into the same Tailscale account); security relies on the pairing token — don't share the code. The target also goes offline when asleep — waking still needs an always-on LAN jump host to send the magic packet.";
"gw.hintTsStopped" = "Tailscale is stopped — connect it from the system tray / menu bar, then click Re-detect.";
"gw.hintTsGuiDown" = "Tailscale is installed but its GUI isn't running — click below to open Tailscale.app (ready when the menu-bar icon appears); it re-detects automatically after a few seconds.";
"gw.openTsApp" = "Open Tailscale.app";
"gw.hintTsOldExt" = "Tailscale is installed, but the old network extension is still “pending uninstall on reboot” — the new extension can't activate and connections keep failing. Restart the Mac and it switches to the new extension automatically; then click Re-detect. (Reinstalling won't help — don't repeatedly uninstall/reinstall.)";
"gw.rebootRecheck" = "Rebooted, re-detect";
"gw.hintTsExtNotAllowed" = "Tailscale is installed, but the network extension isn't allowed yet — until approved it can't reach the network and connecting always fails. Click below to open “System Settings → General → Login Items & Extensions → Network Extensions” and turn on Tailscale (may need fingerprint/password); then click Re-detect.";
"gw.openExtSettings" = "Open network extension settings";
"gw.hintFunnelPublish" = "Publish this machine's service as a public address via the official Tailscale relay (https://machine.ts.net) — phones can access it without installing Tailscale; the address is fixed. Networks in some regions may be unstable and traffic is bandwidth-limited.";
"gw.hintFunnelAuth" = "You need to allow Funnel and enable an HTTPS certificate on the official Tailscale page (Owner/Admin account required); one authorization is long-lived.";
"gw.hintTsLogout" = "Runs tailscale logout: disconnects and clears the local login credentials and saved AuthKey; re-authorization is needed next time. Device records in the Tailscale console must be removed manually.";
"gw.hintTsnPublish" = "No need to install Tailscale — the built-in engine publishes this machine's service as a public address (https://anyboot.….ts.net); phones access it without installing Tailscale, address fixed. The first connection to the coordination server may be unstable in some regions, and traffic via the Tailscale relay is bandwidth-limited.";
"gw.hintTsnAuthKey" = "Issue a one-time device auth key in the Tailscale admin console → Settings → Keys; with it, no browser login when starting the engine.";
"gw.hintTsnLogin" = "Tailscale account login needed — click the button below to authorize in the browser (once is enough, credentials remembered). After login the engine continues automatically; no need to toggle. The engine then initializes environment resources (node config, HTTPS cert, public DNS, etc.), usually a few minutes — check the status or log every few minutes; once ready it shows here and the public address prints in the log.";
