"and.powerIntro" = "Power buttons run immediately, no confirmation — the effects of each are here:";
"and.powerNotes" = "· Sleep = suspend to RAM: wakes almost instantly, but network services stop — this tab shows offline and pages won't load (expected). Wake it with “Wake” (needs MAC + WoL);\\n· Shut down: powers off at once; web service stops — afterwards only “Wake” (needs MAC) or the physical button;\\n· Restart: reboots at once; the web session drops — heartbeat returns online automatically after reboot;\\n· Wake: sends a magic packet to power on; needs MAC and WoL enabled in BIOS.";
"and.powerHowExec" = "How these buttons run (LAN / sol)";
"and.powerExecNote" = "Actions with a “LAN power route” configured send a UDP packet to the route's broadcast addr:port, executed by sol on the target by port — so it works while asleep or with the web service down. Without sol, the packet goes out but nothing runs it.\\nActions without a route use the old path: wake sends standard WOL (magic packet); restart/shutdown/sleep call the computer's web API.";
"and.powerWakeFrom" = "Where the wake packet is sent from:";
"and.powerWakeFromNote" = "· Wake route configured → send to the route's address/port (select specific MACs);\\n· SSH jump host configured → it broadcasts on the intranet (works from outside);\\n· Neither → the phone broadcasts on the LAN (phone must be on the same subnet);\\n· Only “remote access” available (public tunnel while away) → wake can't be sent: a magic packet is a LAN UDP broadcast and can't cross a tunnel. Restart/shutdown/sleep call the web API, which works over the tunnel.";
"and.powerCheck" = "No response — check in order:";
"and.powerCheckNote" = "① Wake on LAN enabled in BIOS (affects wake only);\\n② Using the wired NIC's MAC — most wireless NICs don't support wake-from-off;\\n③ MAC entered on the matching address row in “Edit server” (e.g. 192.168.0.120:12300 AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF);\\n④ Broadcast address/port in the route correct (matching sol's listener);\\n⑤ Target and phone on the same subnet (LAN broadcast only works within it).";
